      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "For the functions $v(x)$ and $w(x),$ you're given the following data:\n\n$$\nv(2)=-3,\\,{v}^{′}(2)=1,\\,w(2)=-2,\\,{w}^{′}(2)=-4\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(v(x)-2w(x))$ at $x=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the sum and constant multiple rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(v(x)-2w(x))={v}^{′}(x)-2{w}^{′}(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(v(x)-2w(x))|}_{x=2} & ={v}^{′}(2)-2{w}^{′}(2) \\\\  & =1-2\\cdot (-4) \\\\  & =1+8 \\\\  & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
